            <ArticleTitle>The Role of the Speech-Language Pathologist in Creating a Model for Interprofessional Practice in an Ambulatory Care Clinic.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-170</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0031-3955(17)30144-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pcl.2017.08.028</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a need to better coordinate services for children in urban settings who are at risk for communication disorders. This article addresses the barriers to obtaining services and discusses the process for creating a model for interprofessional practice to better serve patients from lower socioeconomic backgrounds.</AbstractText>
